<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span><h2>What Are Dry and Wet Scrubbers?</h2><p>Scrubbers are designed to treat polluted exhaust before it is released from an industrial or commercial process. The appropriate technology depends on the type of pollutant, exhaust temperature, airflow, pressure, and operating conditions.</p><p>Dry scrubbers are especially suitable for exhaust streams containing acidic gases and particulates. They can handle high-temperature and highly acidic exhaust streams, making them useful for various production processes. Wet scrubbers use liquid-based treatment to capture contaminants from exhaust air and may be used for fumes, oil, grease, and other pollutants.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h2>Dry Scrubbers</h2><p>Dry scrubbers are a type of industrial pollution control system designed to extract harmful gases and particulates from exhaust streams. They use absorbent materials or chemical reactions rather than water to treat contaminated air.</p><p>The current range includes FAEK-1, FAEK-2, FAEK-3, and FAEK-4 models. A single unit can handle capacity up to 12,000 CFM, while multiple units can be configured for a maximum capacity of up to 60,000 CFM.</p><p>Dry scrubbers are especially useful for processes that generate acidic or high-temperature exhaust. Their applications include pharmaceutical manufacturing, textile processing, asphalt processing, oil and gas, fertilizer manufacturing, metal processing, and other industrial processes.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel" style="grid-column:1/-1"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h2>Wet Scrubbers</h2><p>Wet scrubbers use liquid-based treatment to remove contaminants from exhaust air. In kitchen and process exhaust applications, contaminated fumes are drawn through hoods and treated using high-pressure water jets, which help trap contaminants such as oil and grease.</p><p>The wet scrubber construction includes a double-bank GI spray header with brass/PVC spray nozzles. DIDW centrifugal blowers, TEFC three-phase motors, adjustable motor mounting fixtures, monoblock pumps, and an SS304/GI sump with an FRP tank are also part of the listed construction.</p><p>The system is designed for efficient scrubbing with low pressure drop, making it suitable for applications where continuous exhaust treatment is required.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Dry/Wet Scrubbers</h2><p>Dry and wet scrubbers offer different configurations for different pollution-control requirements. Important features include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Dry and wet scrubbing options</li><li>Dry scrubber models FAEK-1, FAEK-2, FAEK-3 and FAEK-4</li><li>Single dry scrubber capacity up to 12,000 CFM</li><li>Multi-unit dry scrubber capacity up to 60,000 CFM</li><li>Absorbent or chemical treatment for dry scrubbing</li><li>Liquid-based treatment for wet scrubbing</li><li>Double-bank GI spray header</li><li>Brass/PVC spray nozzles</li><li>DIDW centrifugal blowers</li><li>TEFC three-phase motors</li><li>Adjustable motor mounting fixture</li><li>Adjustable taper bush pulleys</li><li>Monoblock pumps</li><li>SS304/GI sump with FRP tank</li><li>Extruded aluminium profile body</li><li>Double-skin PUF panel or single-skin GI casing options</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-tables"><div class="fcx-tablewrap"><table class="fcx-table fcx-table--3"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Dry Scrubber</th><th scope="col">Wet Scrubber</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Models</th><td>FAEK-1, 2, 3, 4</td><td>Application-specific</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Single Unit Capacity</th><td>Up to 12,000 CFM</td><td>Application-specific</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Maximum Multi-Unit Capacity</th><td>Up to 60,000 CFM</td><td>Application-specific</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Scrubbing Method</th><td>Absorbent materials / chemical reaction</td><td>Liquid and water-jet scrubbing</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Frame</th><td>Application-specific</td><td>Extruded Aluminium Profile</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Base</th><td>Application-specific</td><td>Heavy Gauge Base Frame with Cast Aluminium Corners</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Casing</th><td>Application-specific</td><td>Double-Skin PUF Panels / Single-Skin GI</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Spray Header</th><td>—</td><td>Double Bank GI</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Spray Nozzles</th><td>—</td><td>Brass/PVC</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Blowers</th><td>—</td><td>DIDW Centrifugal Blowers</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Motors</th><td>—</td><td>TEFC Three-Phase Motor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pumps</th><td>—</td><td>Monoblock Pumps</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sump</th><td>—</td><td>SS304/GI with FRP Tank</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="fcx-note fcx-note--wide"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>The final scrubber configuration needs to be selected according to airflow, static pressure, pollutant characteristics, exhaust temperature, application, and site conditions.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Applications of Dry/Wet Scrubbers</h2><p><b>Dry/Wet Scrubbers in Ahmedabad</b> can be used across a wide variety of commercial and industrial applications. The current product range covers:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Asphalt processing</li><li>Pharmaceutical production</li><li>Landfills and biogas</li><li>Coating processes</li><li>Textile processing</li><li>Tar removal</li><li>Curing ovens</li><li>Vinyl manufacturing</li><li>Oil and gas</li><li>Acid mist control</li><li>Fertilizer production</li><li>Wastewater treatment</li><li>Steel processing</li><li>Electronics manufacturing</li><li>Food processing</li><li>Cocoa processing</li><li>Chemical exhaust treatment</li><li>Kitchen exhaust treatment</li></ul><p>Ahmedabad and the wider Gujarat industrial belt, including Vatva, Naroda, Changodar, and Sanand, has textile, chemical, pharmaceutical, engineering, and automotive industries. Many of these facilities run continuous processes where reliable exhaust treatment and air movement are important.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Benefits of Dry/Wet Scrubbers</h2></div><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h3>Effective Pollutant Removal</h3><p>Scrubbers are designed to treat contaminated exhaust before it is discharged, helping control gases, fumes, particulates, and other pollutants.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-shapes"></i></span><h3>Dry Treatment Option</h3><p>Dry scrubbers offer a water-free method of treating exhaust gases and particulates, making them appropriate for applications involving acidic and high-temperature exhaust streams.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i></span><h3>Wet Scrubbing</h3><p>Wet scrubbers use water or other liquid solutions to capture contaminants. This makes them suitable for fumes, oil, grease, and other pollutants that may be trapped through liquid contact.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-shapes"></i></span><h3>Flexible Applications</h3><p>The available configurations can be used across pharmaceutical, textile, chemical, food, metal, oil and gas, wastewater, and other industrial processes.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-layer-group"></i></span><h3>Application-Specific Construction</h3><p>Wet scrubbers can include different casing, blower, motor, pump, spray, and sump arrangements according to the requirements of the system.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Dry/Wet Scrubbers Suppliers in Ahmedabad</h2><p>When choosing <b>Dry/Wet Scrubbers Suppliers in Ahmedabad</b>, complete data about the exhaust application should be provided before selecting the equipment. Airflow, static pressure, pollutant type, concentration, exhaust temperature, and operating conditions can all affect an appropriate scrubber configuration.</p><p>For Ahmedabad projects, scrubbers can be required for chemical and pharmaceutical plants, textile facilities, process industries, production units, and kitchen exhaust systems. The system should therefore be selected according to the actual exhaust characteristics instead of using the same configuration for every application.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Dry/Wet Scrubbers Manufacturer in India</h2><p>For projects looking for a <b>Dry/Wet Scrubbers Manufacturer in India</b>, technical sizing is an important part of the equipment selection process. The scrubber must be matched with the specified airflow, static pressure, pollutant characteristics, and operating environment.</p><p>The manufacturing facility is located in Neemrana, Rajasthan. Each unit is selected according to the required airflow, static pressure, and site conditions. Technical sizing and product data can be reviewed before ordering, with completed equipment dispatched to Ahmedabad and other places throughout India.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right Scrubber</h2><p>Before selecting a dry or wet scrubber, consider the following factors:</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Identify the Pollutants:</b> Determine whether the exhaust carries gases, fumes, dust, oil, grease, acid mist, or other contaminants.</li><li><b>Check Airflow:</b> Establish the specified CFM for the exhaust system.</li><li><b>Determine Static Pressure:</b> Consider resistance from ducts, hoods, filters, dampers, and other components.</li><li><b>Select Scrubbing Method:</b> Choose dry or wet technology according to the pollutant and process.</li><li><b>Check Exhaust Temperature:</b> High-temperature applications may also require an appropriate scrubber configuration.</li><li><b>Consider Materials:</b> Select casing, sump, spray nozzles, and other components according to the operating environment.</li><li><b>Review Maintenance:</b> Ensure pumps, blowers, spray systems, and other components may be accessed for inspection and servicing.</li><li><b>Consider Site Conditions:</b> Review available space, installation requirements, and operating conditions before final selection.</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What is a dry scrubber?</summary><p>A dry scrubber is pollution control equipment designed to extract harmful gases and particulates from exhaust streams using absorbent materials or chemical reactions without water.</p></details><details><summary>What is a wet scrubber?</summary><p>A wet scrubber uses liquid-based treatment to capture contaminants from exhaust air. Water jets and spray nozzles can help trap pollutants such as fumes, oil, and grease.</p></details><details><summary>What is the capacity of the dry scrubbers?</summary><p>The listed dry scrubber models can handle up to 12,000 CFM for a single unit and up to 60,000 CFM using multiple units.</p></details><details><summary>Where are dry scrubbers used?</summary><p>Dry scrubbers are used in asphalt processing, pharmaceuticals, textile processing, oil and gas, fertilizer production, metal processing, electronics, food processing, wastewater treatment, and various other applications.</p></details><details><summary>What components are included in wet scrubbers?</summary><p>The listed wet scrubber construction includes an aluminium profile body, GI spray header, brass/PVC spray nozzles, DIDW centrifugal blowers, TEFC 3-phase motors, monoblock pumps, and an SS304/GI sump with FRP tank.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Dry and wet scrubbers provide practical solutions for controlling pollutants from commercial, process, and industrial exhaust systems. Dry scrubbers are suitable for applications involving gases and particulates, such as acidic and high-temperature exhaust, while wet scrubbers use liquid-based treatment for fumes, oil, grease, and other contaminants.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. offers dry and wet scrubber solutions for Ahmedabad and other locations across India, with selection based on airflow, static pressure, pollutant characteristics, application, and site conditions. Technical requirements can be reviewed before ordering to identify a suitable scrubber configuration for the project.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
